From a5af31e646283709436b595beef6b0e8ebac0a7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicholas DeTello <no-reply@detello.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:47:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] platform/x86: acer-wmi: Adopt a Turbo state retained
 across reboot

After a warm reboot the EC keeps its turbo state while the new driver
instance starts without key ownership, so selecting a non-Turbo profile
leaves the firmware's turbo state and the fans in turbo mode. Before
committing a non-Turbo profile request on a turbo_profile model with no
recorded key request and the LED capability present, read the
firmware's turbo state; if it is on, switch turbo mode off together with
the profile change, as if the key had enabled it. The read precedes the
profile write, so a read failure leaves the profile unchanged, and turbo
mode is only switched off once the write succeeded. This does not change
the first key press after such a boot; that remains userspace policy.

The LED capability is checked although the quirk implies it, because
force_caps may have removed it; without the check every non-Turbo
profile write would then fail with -EIO.

Tested on the PT516-52s: after a warm reboot with turbo mode on,
userspace wrote the balanced profile at boot and the next key press
turned turbo mode on, so the retained firmware state had been cleared.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c b/drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c
index 716c0116b..60a722f49 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c
@@ -2320,6 +2320,7 @@ static int
 acer_predator_v4_platform_profile_set(struct device *dev,
 				      enum platform_profile_option profile)
 {
+	bool retained = false;
 	int err, tp;
 
 	switch (profile) {
@@ -2343,6 +2344,18 @@ acer_predator_v4_platform_profile_set(struct device *dev,
 	}
 
 	mutex_lock(&acer_turbo_lock);
+	/*
+	 * Read before committing a profile change so errors leave it unchanged.
+	 * force_caps may have removed the LED capability.
+	 */
+	if (tp != ACER_PREDATOR_V4_THERMAL_PROFILE_TURBO &&
+	    quirks->turbo_profile && !turbo_key_profile &&
+	    has_cap(ACER_CAP_TURBO_LED)) {
+		err = acer_get_turbo_led(&retained);
+		if (err)
+			goto out;
+	}
+
 	err = WMID_gaming_set_misc_setting(ACER_WMID_MISC_SETTING_PLATFORM_PROFILE, tp);
 	if (err)
 		goto out;
@@ -2350,8 +2363,11 @@ acer_predator_v4_platform_profile_set(struct device *dev,
 	if (tp != ACER_PREDATOR_V4_THERMAL_PROFILE_TURBO) {
 		last_non_turbo_profile = tp;
 
-		/* Leaving the Turbo profile also ends turbo mode set by the key. */
-		if (turbo_key_profile) {
+		/*
+		 * Leaving the Turbo profile also ends turbo mode set by the key
+		 * or retained by the firmware across a reboot.
+		 */
+		if (turbo_key_profile || retained) {
 			turbo_key_profile = false;
 			acer_set_turbo(false);
 		}
-- 
